# ── Mirror publication allowlist — gate G1 (spec 07 §8.4, SC-6) ──────────────
#
# Glob patterns of the ONLY paths permitted in the public mirror
# (github.com/keel-trade/keel-trade). On EVERY sync — tag push and manual
# dispatch alike — every file in the staged public tree (excluding the
# checkout's own .git/) must match at least one pattern below. Any unmatched
# file turns the sync red BEFORE anything is pushed. Fail-closed: this
# manifest inverts the trust direction — the rsync exclude list is a first
# filter; this file is the boundary.
#
# Adding a new public file class REQUIRES a same-PR edit here — loud by
# construction.
#
# Semantics: Python fnmatch globs, case-sensitive, matched against
# posix paths relative to the staged-tree root by
# .github/scripts/mirror_gates.py. NOTE: fnmatch `*` matches across `/`,
# so `keel/*.py` covers every .py file nested anywhere under keel/.
#
# This file is intentionally published (self-allowlisted, first entry): it
# names only public paths, and publishing it makes the publication boundary
# third-party-auditable.
.mirror-allowlist
.mirror-import-denylist
# Gitleaks config for the G2 secret scan (auto-discovered at the staged-tree
# root by `gitleaks dir`): default rules + scoped false-positive allowlists.
# Published so the scan boundary is auditable alongside the allowlist.
.gitleaks.toml
# ── Repo meta (public-overlay + SDK root) ────────────────────────────────────
.gitignore
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*.md
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
README.md
glama.json
pyproject.toml
# ── SDK package code + bundled data ──────────────────────────────────────────
keel/*.py
keel/data/*.json
keel/data/knowledge/*.md
keel/data/patterns/*.md
keel/data/reference/*.md
keel/skills/*/SKILL.md
# MCP-Apps card widget assets (client-rendered card JS/CSS/HTML templates).
# Intentionally public: they ship in the PyPI wheel already, and DP2
# (no client-side analytics — publicly verifiable in the mirror) REQUIRES
# the widget source be mirrorable. Per-extension (not a bare dir wildcard)
# so a new asset file class still reddens G1 loudly.
keel/widgets/assets/*.js
keel/widgets/assets/*.css
keel/widgets/assets/*.html.tmpl
pipeline_engine/*.py
# The clock alphabet (libs/timeframes), vendored verbatim into the SDK by
# build_data.py since 9051d97d0 and shipped in the wheel (pyproject
# `packages = [..., "timeframes"]`): the bundled validator re-exports
# TIMEFRAME_MINUTES from it, so the wheel is already public with it and the
# mirror would otherwise publish an importable pipeline_engine that dies on
# `from timeframes import ...`. Stdlib-only, no secrets. Per-extension, so a
# new file class under it still reddens G1 loudly.
timeframes/*.py
# Generated lookup tables the bundled validator READS at runtime (M4 clock
# work made the DSL subset carry them). Same derivation as the already-public
# registry.json/type_graph.json — public component registry in, tables out; no
# secrets. Publishing the validator sources without the data they load would
# ship a non-functional package. Per-extension, so a new data class still
# reddens G1 loudly.
pipeline_engine/dsl/fixtures/*.json
scripts/*.py
scripts/icon.png
scripts/manifest.template.json
# The MCP-Apps card preview harness (Q-1505): a dev script beside the card
# assets it renders, published with them for the same DP2 reason (per-file,
# not a bare *.mjs glob, so a new script class still reddens G1 loudly).
scripts/card_preview.mjs
# Its shared host context (Q-1718): card_preview.mjs imports it, so the
# published preview script cannot run without it.
scripts/card_host_context.mjs
tests/*.py
# Card fixtures (mcp-strategy-view M2.5): the graph JSON the strategy-card
# tests render — including the real HRP pipeline that is the acceptance case
# for the branch packer and the block budget. Published with the tests that
# load them; per-directory, so a new fixture class still reddens G1 loudly.
tests/fixtures/cards/*.json
# The strategy card's rendering guard: the card's contract is a rendered
# DOM (block budget, collapsed parallel, marks), so its assertions live in
# a Playwright script beside the fixtures it drives. Published with the
# test that runs it; per-directory, so a new script class reddens G1.
tests/fixtures/cards/*.mjs
# The channel contract's recorded envelopes (agent-surface-cleanup spec 02
# §2.3: the listed server's own results, presigned URLs redacted) and the
# window display-parity fixture shared with keel-app (spec 03 guard 12).
# Published with the tests that load them; per-file-class, so a new fixture
# class still reddens G1.
tests/fixtures/channels/*.json
tests/fixtures/window-parity.fixture.json
# Recorded tool-result payloads (spec 02 §2.3) the channel-budget replay guard
# reads; staging identity ids are scrubbed to same-length placeholders.
tests/fixtures/payloads/*.json
